WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:04.660 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  welcome to the future future  trials fusion blast you with a cheesy  energetic song when you fire it up it's  so catchy and so ridiculous that I  switched between loving it sincerely and  ironically a hundred different times but  I do love it and it sets the mood  wonderfully for the insane events that  are about to unfold trials fusion so  beautifully melds goofiness with tough  as nails racing that it's hard to wipe  the smile from your face as you crash  repeatedly on your way to victory so  what's changed from the previous trials  games not much you once again find  yourself on 2d tracks complete with all  manner of ramps and obstacles except now  you're in a post-apocalyptic landscape  which man and machine have finally  merged or fused so you need only worry  about managing your acceleration and  leaning such simple tasks prove  consistently difficult and engaging  because of the fantastic course design  as you drive through the first half of  trials fusion perfection is in your  sights just keep your momentum as you  land tricky jumps to shave seconds off  your time and avoid embarrassing  pratfalls  beginner easy and medium difficulties  rope you in with their creative layouts  and enticing aesthetics and there's an  innate Pole to better your score you're  not going to let the ghost representing  your buddy get the better of you are you  although there is a multiplayer mode  it's the leaderboard challenges that  provide the best competition so you lean  and gun the throttle like a pro recently  navigating the bumpy roads the finish  line  it's when you enter the hard courses  that trials takes on a different feeling  the dreams of catching your friend or  finishing without one crash have  evaporated now it's just about survival  seemingly impossible jumps await you and  it takes all your nerve and dedication  to overcome their nastiness  instantaneous restarts pop you back on  the track without a moment to breathe  and the minutes fly by before you even  realize it it's mind over matter what  anyone can triumph if they have the  patience  I hit both the literal and figurative  wall towards the tail under the hard  tracks but I didn't let getting stuck  stop me from having fun so I went back  to my old stomping grounds to improve my  times whereas I struggled in some of  those early tracks now ow is more skill  I could keep my speed and balance  throughout trials fusion is built  entirely on your abilities there's no  luck here nothing cheap or unfair so  when you do achieve a perfect run or  fast a devious track you feel as el  you've earned it and when I'm left back  to those hard tracks I finally cross the  finish line tricks and previous trials  games were limited to dangerous front  and back flutes and now you can perform  even crazier boots and their tracks  designed just for your lunacy by just  using the right stick you can perform  masochistic maneuvers that would make  your mom sick holding a Superman pose  until the last possible second shows  your guile and ieave it a but landing  that trick feels so good that it's worth  pushing yourself as far as your rider  can go there are challenges on every  course to give you a bevy of unique  objectives - some require raw skills  such as not leaning throughout a run  whereas others about exploration where  are the flowers hidden and others well  bring your barf bag unless you enjoy  playing upside down challenges do a  great job of mixing up how to play and  give you an exciting detour when you're  struggling in a standard race trials  fusion is an excellent representation of  the fantastic racing that this series  has become known for sharp controls and  understandable physics keep success  formally in your hands and the diversity  in the courses ratchet up the surprises  and forces you to use all of your  abilities  the one place fuse and stumbles is in  its creation tools incredible powers at  your fingertips  it's just harnessing it that's a problem  there's no in-game tutorial instead  you're pointed towards a YouTube page  the tools themselves are unintuitive and  then the course is glitchy it's all too  easy to fall into the ground or get  stuck on or off which means you have to  go back to the drawing board a lot to  iron out those kinks those who love  creating courses will be able to conjure  up amazing experiences  but the barrier for entry is far too  high for those who just want to play  around still for those who love  competing trows fusion is another great  entry in the franchise from the goofy  intro song to the rag doll crashes  you'll laugh throughout but it takes  dedication and skill to master the many  courses welcome to the future just  beware of stray missiles  [Music]

